          This patient has been diagnosed with Pelvic Venous Disorder (PeVD), a recognized clinical entity supported by the Society of Interventional Radiology, American Vein & Lymphatic Society, and American Venous Forum. Ovarian vein embolization is a minimally invasive, evidence-based treatment for symptomatic PeVD.

          Supporting Evidence:

• Ovarian vein embolization (OVE) is a minimally invasive, evidence-based procedure for Pelvic Venous Disorder (PeVD)

• Multiple systematic reviews demonstrate significant symptom relief and improved quality of life

• Society of Interventional Radiology (SIR) supports OVE as medically necessary for PeVD

• Published efficacy data shows 70-80% symptom improvement at 12-month follow-up

• Procedure has low complication rates and excellent safety profile

